The function is already a minimal inlined field lookup, so I kept the exact semantics but collapsed the null check and validity call into a single conditional return expression, which lets the compiler emit a tighter branch/select sequence without changing any return value.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsOpponentScoreValid() const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(8);
        return (FIT_NULL != field) ? field->IsValueValid() : FIT_FALSE;
    }
```